# The raw client assets are the photographic and video masters (26–52 MB each,
# ~1.3 GB total). They are the source for scripts/process-assets.mjs and must
# never be uploaded to Vercel — only the processed output in assets-web/ and
# public/ is deployed.
#
# NOTE THE LEADING SLASHES. They are essential, not tidiness.
#
# Without one, a pattern matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, and the
# matching is case-insensitive. So a bare "Gallery/" silently also excluded
# src/components/gallery/, src/app/(frontend)/gallery/ and assets-web/gallery/ —
# which broke the production build with a module-not-found on GalleryGrid, while
# the local build was perfectly fine.
#
# scripts/check-vercelignore.mjs enforces this; it runs as part of `pnpm verify`.
/Gallery/
/Homepage pic combo/
/Starting video/

# Working folders used while building the site.
/.research/
/.scaffold/

# The original logo artwork. The traced SVG in public/brand is what ships.
/logo.jpeg

# Never ship local secrets. Git-ignored already, so this only matters for a
# `vercel` CLI deploy from a working copy.
/.env
/.env.local
